{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02522",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.11,
      "end_seconds": 4.08,
      "duration_seconds": 2.97,
      "text": "Right, thanks for waiting, come in."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 5.36,
      "end_seconds": 9.23,
      "duration_seconds": 3.87,
      "text": "Hmm, hello. I hope I'm not late."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 10.59,
      "end_seconds": 15.43,
      "duration_seconds": 4.84,
      "text": "hello, doctor i'm here with them in case I can help"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 17.01,
      "end_seconds": 22.58,
      "duration_seconds": 5.57,
      "text": "Absolutely, come and sit beside them. Tell me what's brought you in."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 23.27,
      "end_seconds": 26.49,
      "duration_seconds": 3.22,
      "text": "we came because of aching all over"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 31.41,
      "end_seconds": 34.58,
      "duration_seconds": 3.17,
      "text": "How much trouble does it give you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 36.67,
      "end_seconds": 37.62,
      "duration_seconds": 0.95,
      "text": "Mostly severe."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 39.0,
      "end_seconds": 41.89,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "Is it it worse at certain times?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 43.86,
      "end_seconds": 48.19,
      "duration_seconds": 4.33,
      "text": "Stress and cold weather definitely sets it off."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 49.64,
      "end_seconds": 52.98,
      "duration_seconds": 3.34,
      "text": "So, is it constant or in episodes?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 54.38,
      "end_seconds": 57.24,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "It It just comes and goes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 58.89,
      "end_seconds": 62.88,
      "duration_seconds": 3.99,
      "text": "what do you do to to make it better?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 64.29,
      "end_seconds": 66.98,
      "duration_seconds": 2.69,
      "text": "I get some relief from heat."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 68.21,
      "end_seconds": 71.04,
      "duration_seconds": 2.83,
      "text": "Have you noticed anything else alongside it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 72.47,
      "end_seconds": 82.99,
      "duration_seconds": 10.52,
      "text": "When it starts I tend to get poor concentration as well. As for poor concentration, mostly moderate. I've also had tender spots."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 84.76,
      "end_seconds": 89.95,
      "duration_seconds": 5.19,
      "text": "Have you had aching all over before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 91.63,
      "end_seconds": 101.41,
      "duration_seconds": 9.78,
      "text": "Let me think, yes, something like this happened last year, and and it went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 102.82,
      "end_seconds": 104.97,
      "duration_seconds": 2.15,
      "text": "Has there been any rash?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 105.49,
      "end_seconds": 108.33,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "not that I've noticed, no rash"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 109.78,
      "end_seconds": 113.52,
      "duration_seconds": 3.74,
      "text": "Did you get joint swelling, fever or weight loss?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 118.12,
      "end_seconds": 120.49,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "Nope, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 120.85,
      "end_seconds": 123.66,
      "duration_seconds": 2.81,
      "text": "mm-hmm. How's your breathing otherwise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 125.48,
      "end_seconds": 126.39,
      "duration_seconds": 0.91,
      "text": "breathing's normal"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 127.94,
      "end_seconds": 132.25,
      "duration_seconds": 4.31,
      "text": "Anything with your heart, like skipped beats or fainting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 134.26,
      "end_seconds": 137.06,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "no, nothing with my heart"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 138.81,
      "end_seconds": 141.0,
      "duration_seconds": 2.19,
      "text": "Tell me your medicines, please."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 142.35,
      "end_seconds": 152.54,
      "duration_seconds": 10.19,
      "text": "Febuxostat. I take it 80 milligrams, once a day for the gout. Simvastatin, 20 milligrams, maybe, at night."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 154.41,
      "end_seconds": 158.32,
      "duration_seconds": 3.91,
      "text": "Have you got the box or the prescription on you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 159.58,
      "end_seconds": 165.53,
      "duration_seconds": 5.95,
      "text": "No, it's at home. It's paracetamol, 1 gram, when needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 177.08,
      "end_seconds": 179.28,
      "duration_seconds": 2.2,
      "text": "Any surgery in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 180.1,
      "end_seconds": 185.79,
      "duration_seconds": 5.69,
      "text": "Just a cataract operation in my left eye, about a year ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 186.86,
      "end_seconds": 189.22,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "Do you live by yourself?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 190.14,
      "end_seconds": 194.67,
      "duration_seconds": 4.53,
      "text": "No, I share a house with my brother."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 196.14,
      "end_seconds": 198.39,
      "duration_seconds": 2.25,
      "text": "do you get out much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 199.87,
      "end_seconds": 204.5,
      "duration_seconds": 4.63,
      "text": "Not much, I mostly stay in these days"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 205.06,
      "end_seconds": 208.85,
      "duration_seconds": 3.79,
      "text": "Let me ask about allergies, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 210.78,
      "end_seconds": 213.59,
      "duration_seconds": 2.81,
      "text": "No, I'm not allergic to anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 230.52,
      "end_seconds": 233.11,
      "duration_seconds": 2.59,
      "text": "do you have any long-term conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 234.65,
      "end_seconds": 240.24,
      "duration_seconds": 5.59,
      "text": "I've, I've had gout for five years now. Yes, high cholesterol."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 245.89,
      "end_seconds": 251.71,
      "duration_seconds": 5.82,
      "text": "Okay, I can see gout and high cholesterol in your file as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 265.0,
      "end_seconds": 267.54,
      "duration_seconds": 2.54,
      "text": "let me take your readings now"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 280.77,
      "end_seconds": 282.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.02,
      "text": "Sit still for a moment..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 303.24,
      "end_seconds": 313.61,
      "duration_seconds": 10.37,
      "text": "okay: temperature is 36.9 degrees, pulse 85. And oxygen saturation is 98 percent, pressure 122 over 78, respiratory rate 15."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 316.05,
      "end_seconds": 321.67,
      "duration_seconds": 5.62,
      "text": "I'll need to to examine you for this, it won't take long."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 325.21,
      "end_seconds": 326.19,
      "duration_seconds": 0.98,
      "text": "That's alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 327.11,
      "end_seconds": 329.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.32,
      "text": "Hold that for a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 341.63,
      "end_seconds": 347.82,
      "duration_seconds": 6.19,
      "text": "Your joints are not swollen and you are tender over many muscle points."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 350.98,
      "end_seconds": 364.36,
      "duration_seconds": 13.38,
      "text": "That's the examination finished. Putting it all together, it points towards fibromyalgia. I want to be honest that this is an impression, not a final answer. I can't rule out polymyalgia yet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 366.43,
      "end_seconds": 367.93,
      "duration_seconds": 1.5,
      "text": "Is this permanent?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 368.53,
      "end_seconds": 380.71,
      "duration_seconds": 12.18,
      "text": "nothing I've seen today points to an emergency it looks like fibromyalgia, but I'd like to confirm. Blood tests is what I'd like next, for widespread pain"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 382.01,
      "end_seconds": 383.82,
      "duration_seconds": 1.81,
      "text": "That's fine with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 385.9,
      "end_seconds": 412.35,
      "duration_seconds": 26.45,
      "text": "The treatment will be amitriptyline, 10 milligrams, at night, long term. You take it by mouth. That's for pain and sleep. Gentle graded exercise such as swimming helps more than rest. Let's get you seen by the pain clinic, I'll arrange the letter. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 414.4,
      "end_seconds": 416.49,
      "duration_seconds": 2.09,
      "text": "Thank you, that's clear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 417.85,
      "end_seconds": 420.53,
      "duration_seconds": 2.68,
      "text": "That's all from me. Any questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 422.36,
      "end_seconds": 424.55,
      "duration_seconds": 2.19,
      "text": "Alright, thanks, take care."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 426.35,
      "end_seconds": 427.69,
      "duration_seconds": 1.34,
      "text": "Goodbye for now."
    }
  ]
}